{"obs_mqv8pfsd_10d77bcb6164":{"observation":{"hookType":"session_updated","id":"obs_mqv8pfsd_10d77bcb6164","raw":{"additions":null,"deletions":null,"files":null,"parentID":"ses_0fb0da627ffe1MoEyui2GTY7HI","title":"Fix graph_store + graph_extractor (@languages/python-pro subagent)"},"sessionId":"ses_0fae5dfd6ffes8nhx5eGrq5TbX","timestamp":"2026-06-26T18:03:46.091Z"},"type":"raw"},"obs_mqv8pfsg_6ab921e476c2":{"observation":{"hookType":"prompt_submit","id":"obs_mqv8pfsg_6ab921e476c2","raw":{"agent":"languages/python-pro","files":[],"model":{"modelID":"big-pickle","providerID":"opencode"},"parts_summary":["text"],"prompt":"Fix 3 critical bugs in the xnch memory module.\n\n**Bug 1: /Users/xnch/xnchSystems/xnch/xnch/memory/graph_store.py â€” upsert_relation sync**\nRead the file first.\n- Make `upsert_relation` async (it's currently sync but called from async contexts):\n  - Change `def upsert_relation` to `async def upsert_relation`\n  - The `create_memory` call inside it needs no change (it's sync but the function needs to be awaitable)\n  - If `self._relationship_store` is not None, change the `self._relationship_store.upsert_relationship(...)` call to `await self._relationship_store.upsert_relationship(...)`\n- Fix `upsert_entity` similarly if it has the same sync issue (check callers).\n- Currently uses `asyncio.get_running_loop().create_task()` pattern for the dual-write. Simplify to direct call since we're making it async.\n\n**Bug 2: /Users/xnch/xnchSystems/xnch/xnch/memory/graph_store.py â€” duplicate relations**\n- `upsert_relation` always calls `create_memory()` unconditionally â€” no dedup check. Every call creates a new duplicate record. Fix: Add dedup:\n```python\nexisting = search_memory(RELATIONS_CATEGORY, rel_text, n_results=5)\nmatch = next((r for r in existing if r[\"metadata\"].get(\"from_id\") == from_id\n              and r[\"metadata\"].get(\"to_id\") == to_id\n              and r[\"metadata\"].get(\"rel_type\") == rel_type), None)\nif match:\n    update_memory(RELATIONS_CATEGORY, match[\"id\"], metadata={...})\nelse:\n    create_memory(RELATIONS_CATEGORY, rel_text, metadata={...})\n```\nYou'll need to add `search_memory, update_memory` to the imports.\n\n**Bug 3: /Users/xnch/xnchSystems/xnch/xnch/memory/graph_extractor.py**\nRead the file first.\n- Line 36-37: GraphStore() instantiated without relationship_store. Fix:\n  - Accept `relationship_store` as optional parameter in `extract_and_store()`\n  - Pass it to `GraphStore(relationship_store=relationship_store)`\n- Line 72: Model hardcoded to \"ollama/phi3:mini\". Fix to use config:\n  - Add `from ..config import settings` \n  - Use `model=settings.graph_extractor_model` (already exists in config.py)\n\nReturn a summary of every change (file, line, what changed).","variant":null},"sessionId":"ses_0fae5dfd6ffes8nhx5eGrq5TbX","timestamp":"2026-06-26T18:03:46.094Z","userPrompt":"Fix 3 critical bugs in the xnch memory module.\n\n**Bug 1: /Users/xnch/xnchSystems/xnch/xnch/memory/graph_store.py â€” upsert_relation sync**\nRead the file first.\n- Make `upsert_relation` async (it's currently sync but called from async contexts):\n  - Change `def upsert_relation` to `async def upsert_relation`\n  - The `create_memory` call inside it needs no change (it's sync but the function needs to be awaitable)\n  - If `self._relationship_store` is not None, change the `self._relationship_store.upsert_relationship(...)` call to `await self._relationship_store.upsert_relationship(...)`\n- Fix `upsert_entity` similarly if it has the same sync issue (check callers).\n- Currently uses `asyncio.get_running_loop().create_task()` pattern for the dual-write. Simplify to direct call since we're making it async.\n\n**Bug 2: /Users/xnch/xnchSystems/xnch/xnch/memory/graph_store.py â€” duplicate relations**\n- `upsert_relation` always calls `create_memory()` unconditionally â€” no dedup check. Every call creates a new duplicate record. Fix: Add dedup:\n```python\nexisting = search_memory(RELATIONS_CATEGORY, rel_text, n_results=5)\nmatch = next((r for r in existing if r[\"metadata\"].get(\"from_id\") == from_id\n              and r[\"metadata\"].get(\"to_id\") == to_id\n              and r[\"metadata\"].get(\"rel_type\") == rel_type), None)\nif match:\n    update_memory(RELATIONS_CATEGORY, match[\"id\"], metadata={...})\nelse:\n    create_memory(RELATIONS_CATEGORY, rel_text, metadata={...})\n```\nYou'll need to add `search_memory, update_memory` to the imports.\n\n**Bug 3: /Users/xnch/xnchSystems/xnch/xnch/memory/graph_extractor.py**\nRead the file first.\n- Line 36-37: GraphStore() instantiated without relationship_store. Fix:\n  - Accept `relationship_store` as optional parameter in `extract_and_store()`\n  - Pass it to `GraphStore(relationship_store=relationship_store)`\n- Line 72: Model hardcoded to \"ollama/phi3:mini\". Fix to use config:\n  - Add `from ..config import settings` \n  - Use `model=settings.graph_extractor_model` (already exists in config.py)\n\nReturn a summary of every change (file, line, what changed)."},"type":"raw"},"obs_mqv8pfsx_03add074e0be":{"observation":{"hookType":"session_status","id":"obs_mqv8pfsx_03add074e0be","raw":{"attempt":null,"message":"","status_type":"busy"},"sessionId":"ses_0fae5dfd6ffes8nhx5eGrq5TbX","timestamp":"2026-06-26T18:03:46.112Z"},"type":"raw"},"obs_mqv8pfsy_c8469e42ef64":{"observation":{"hookType":"assistant_message","id":"obs_mqv8pfsy_c8469e42ef64","raw":{"cost":0,"duration_ms":null,"error":null,"finish":null,"messageID":"msg_f051a2041001PmqLn0h0VLtQ6Z","mode":"languages/python-pro","modelID":"big-pickle","parentID":"msg_f051a202d001RdPteunQMhBf24","providerID":"opencode","tokens":{"cache_read":0,"cache_write":0,"input":0,"output":0,"reasoning":0}},"sessionId":"ses_0fae5dfd6ffes8nhx5eGrq5TbX","timestamp":"2026-06-26T18:03:46.113Z"},"type":"raw"},"obs_mqv8pfwc_53bdfc2a8e04":{"observation":{"hookType":"session_diff","id":"obs_mqv8pfwc_53bdfc2a8e04","raw":{"additions":0,"deletions":0,"diffs":[],"files":[]},"sessionId":"ses_0fae5dfd6ffes8nhx5eGrq5TbX","timestamp":"2026-06-26T18:03:46.235Z"},"type":"raw"},"obs_mqv8pfwn_fda4a7c67f7f":{"observation":{"hookType":"llm_params","id":"obs_mqv8pfwn_fda4a7c67f7f","raw":{"agent":"languages/python-pro","context_limit":200000,"cost_1k_input":0,"cost_1k_output":0,"max_output_tokens":32000,"model":"opencode/big-pickle","provider_url":"https://opencode.ai/zen/v1"},"sessionId":"ses_0fae5dfd6ffes8nhx5eGrq5TbX","timestamp":"2026-06-26T18:03:46.246Z"},"type":"raw"},"obs_mqv8pht4_df2d0550c609":{"observation":{"concepts":["system metadata"],"confidence":0.9,"facts":["Current timestamp: 2026-06-26T18:03:48.710Z","Reasoning hook initialized"],"files":[],"id":"obs_mqv8pht4_df2d0550c609","importance":1,"narrative":"The system recorded a timestamp and a reasoning hook. No specific tool usage or file changes were present in this input.","sessionId":"ses_0fae5dfd6ffes8nhx5eGrq5TbX","subtitle":"Timestamp and reasoning hook recorded","timestamp":"2026-06-26T18:03:48.710Z","title":"System Timestamp Update","type":"other"},"type":"compressed"},"obs_mqv8piaa_9f0ffeb42e25":{"observation":{"concepts":["semantic graph store","entity-relationship modeling","layered memory architecture"],"confidence":1,"facts":["GraphStore implements Layer 3 memory using agentmemory categories.","Uses 'entities' and 'relations' categories for semantic storage.","upsert_entity handles deduplication by searching for existing entity IDs.","upsert_relation creates/updates relationship strings and optionally updates an external relationship_store.","Dependencies include agentmemory (create_memory, search_memory, get_memories, update_memory)."],"files":["/Users/xnch/xnchSystems/xnch/xnch/memory/graph_store.py"],"id":"obs_mqv8piaa_9f0ffeb42e25","importance":4,"narrative":"The agent read the graph_store.py file to understand how the semantic graph is constructed and how entities and relations are persisted using the agentmemory backend.","sessionId":"ses_0fae5dfd6ffes8nhx5eGrq5T