e files may have been recently added without a commit or are not part of the checked history.","sessionId":"ses_0fae5dfd6ffes8nhx5eGrq5TbX","subtitle":"Investigating creation timestamps of graph store and extractor","timestamp":"2026-06-26T18:04:34.532Z","title":"Check git history for memory components","type":"command_run"},"type":"compressed"},"obs_mqv8qkf4_34dabf31b879":{"observation":{"concepts":["pytest execution","python environment configuration","unit testing"],"confidence":0.9,"facts":["Command failed because pytest module is not found in the current python environment.","Python path: /opt/homebrew/opt/python@3.14/bin/python3.14"],"files":["xnch/tests/test_graph_store.py"],"id":"obs_mqv8qkf4_34dabf31b879","importance":4,"narrative":"Attempted to run the graph store test suite using pytest, but the execution failed because the pytest module is not installed in the active Python 3.14 environment. This prevents verification of the graph store implementation.","sessionId":"ses_0fae5dfd6ffes8nhx5eGrq5TbX","subtitle":"Executing pytest for xnch/tests/test_graph_store.py","timestamp":"2026-06-26T18:04:38.750Z","title":"Run graph store tests","type":"command_run"},"type":"compressed"},"obs_mqv8qktm_8b3b9b7cc6ce":{"observation":{"concepts":["git history tracking","file lineage"],"confidence":0.9,"facts":["Command executed: git log --all --diff-filter=A --follow --format=\"%H %ad %s\" -- xnch/xnch/memory/graph_store.py","Target file: xnch/xnch/memory/graph_store.py"],"files":["xnch/xnch/memory/graph_store.py"],"id":"obs_mqv8qktm_8b3b9b7cc6ce","importance":3,"narrative":"The user attempted to retrieve the git history specifically for additions to graph_store.py to understand its origin. The command yielded no output, suggesting the file might not have been newly added in the tracked commits or the command scope was too specific.","sessionId":"ses_0fae5dfd6ffes8nhx5eGrq5TbX","subtitle":"Checking file creation/addition history","timestamp":"2026-06-26T18:04:39.273Z","title":"Git history investigation for graph_store.py","type":"command_run"},"type":"compressed"},"obs_mqv8qp41_6e315f5d7afd":{"observation":{"concepts":["GraphStore unit testing","mocking memory operations","entity-relation modeling","pytest fixtures"],"confidence":1,"facts":["Tests cover upserting entities, updating entities, and retrieving entities by name.","Tests include asynchronous relation upserting using `upsert_relation`.","Uses `unittest.mock.patch` to mock `search_memory`, `create_memory`, and `update_memory`.","Verifies graph path isolation logic."],"files":["/Users/xnch/xnchSystems/xnch/tests/test_graph_store.py"],"id":"obs_mqv8qp41_6e315f5d7afd","importance":3,"narrative":"The user read the test suite for GraphStore to understand the expected behavior and interface of the memory graph implementation, specifically focusing on entity and relation management.","sessionId":"ses_0fae5dfd6ffes8nhx5eGrq5TbX","subtitle":"Inspecting unit tests for GraphStore implementation","timestamp":"2026-06-26T18:04:44.825Z","title":"Read test_graph_store.py","type":"file_read"},"type":"compressed"}}␀␀¢*␀\µÿÿ